  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "It would be helpful to have the ability to create a persistent group instance and a counter to the group icon indicating how many available instances there are, that would incentivate people to find new places to go and use the groups feature more.\n\nRight now, the only way to join a group instance is to wait for someone to create one or create your own, if that option is even available, and no one wants to create groups instances because they would have to sit there alone hoping people will join them, even if you use the announcement feature.\n\nBy creating a persistent group instance, that instance would always exist and be joinable even if there's nobody in it, like a public instance, except only visible to members of the group that instance belongs to. It would give members a common place to meet up without the need to wait for someone to create an instance for that specific group. Adding a counter would also make it easier for people to see how many group instances are available.\n\nI believe that adding this feature would give more meaning to groups, because it would give an extra place for people to go and meet people of similar interests. Right now most people are using groups to have a fancy banner on their nameplate.",
